---
// 404 — what nginx serves, with a real 404 status, for a path that doesn't exist.
//
// WHY THIS PAGE HAD TO EXIST BEFORE THE NGINX FIX. The vhost's `location /` ended
// `try_files $uri $uri/ $uri/index.html /index.html`, so every miss returned the HOMEPAGE at
// status **200**. Two costs, and the first is what surfaced it:
//   1. `/favicon.ico` is requested by browsers on their own, at a fixed path, before any markup
//      says where to look. It got 15 kB of HTML typed `text/html`, failed to decode as an image,
//      and the browser drew its own placeholder tile — a square. That was the "i swear it has a
//      square?" bug, and the square was never in favicon.svg.
//   2. A 200 on a miss tells a crawler the URL is real, so any typo'd or stale link becomes an
//      indexable duplicate of the homepage.
// Changing the fallback to `=404` without this page would answer with nginx's own grey default —
// so the page comes first, then the config points at it.
//
// NOT AN `Entry`, same as /style/, /system/ and /resume/: it must never appear in the Work or
// Experiments matrix. It hand-rolls its panel rather than calling `PanelHead`, because `metaOf()`
// throws for an href that isn't in experiments.ts — but the FIGURE is imported like everywhere
// else. (resume.astro hand-copied the SVG and went stale; see MarkFigure.astro.)
//
// NO SEARCH BOX, NO SUGGESTIONS, NO "did you mean". There are fifteen pages and the index lists
// all of them, so the honest recovery is a link to the index — one step, and the reader can see
// the whole site from there. A search field on a fifteen-page site is a control that exists to
// look helpful.
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import MarkFigure from '../components/MarkFigure.astro';
---

<!-- `noindex` because a 404 body should never be indexed even if a crawler follows a link to it.
     The status does most of that work; this covers the case the page is fetched directly. -->
<Layout
  title="Not found — Andrew Shiau"
  description="That page doesn't exist. The index lists everything on the site."
  noindex={true}
>
  <div class="grid">
    <div class="pin">
      <p class="smark">
        <a class="smark-home" href="/"><MarkFigure side="both" />Andrew Shiau</a>
      </p>
      <h1>Not found</h1>

      <div class="facts">
        <div class="frow">
          <div class="fm">What happened</div>
          <div class="ftx">There's nothing at this address. The link was wrong, or it pointed at
            something that has since moved.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="frow">
          <div class="fm">Where to go</div>
          <div class="ftx">The <a href="/">index</a> lists every page on the site — the work, the
            experiments, and the spec.</div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <p class="pfoot">Contact
        <a href="mailto:hi@andrewshiau.com">hi@andrewshiau.com</a>
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="splitrule" aria-hidden="true"></div>

    <div class="feed">
      <p class="fine">
        <a href="/">← Back to the index</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
